      "text": "Perry takes its name from Commodore Oliver Hazard Perry, honored for his 1813 Lake Erie victory.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perry%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Founded in 1817, Perry County’s history stretches back to the early 19th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.perrycountyohio.us/perry-county-ohio/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Ohio’s only national forest, Wayne National Forest, occupies more than one‑fifth of Perry County’s land.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.perrycountyohio.us/perry-county-ohio/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The county sits on an unglaciated Appalachian plateau, giving it craggy cliffs and green valleys unlike Ohio’s flat plains.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.perrycountyohio.us/perry-county-ohio/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Before the Civil War, Perry County was a thriving iron‑production center that boosted local prosperity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.perrycountyohio.us/perry-county-ohio/"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Coal mining lore and tight‑knit Appalachian communities have kept Perry County’s heritage alive through time.",
